# MAIOS reply style

Follow `prompt-kits/AGENT.md` section Reply style (kit 1.8.4). Desktop
SoR is `RESPONSE-STYLE.md` rev g. Do not mix adapters.

Pick one adapter. Do not mix.

- Cursor IDE chat (not Slack): RICH. Optional lead Ready / Waiting /
  Blocked. Lanes as needed: On you / On system / Blocked / Parked /
  Next. Plain language; do not force OK/HOLD/BLOCK. Pair emoji with the
  lead word only. Soft cap 250 prose words unless Meshal asked for a
  document. End with `### Next`; `### Notes` only if non-empty.
- Slack threads: SLACK. Follow `docs/governance/slack-agent-voice.md`.
  No pipe tables. No emoji status rows.
- Terminal / CI / Codex CLI: CLI. ASCII only. [Ready]/[Waiting]/[Blocked].

Hard rules: no em dash, no preamble, no closing offer, no invented
metrics. Mark gaps `[need this:]`. No send, spend, publish, delete,
commit, PR creation/closure, merge, approve, git push, or secret
rotation without a scoped `Approve: <verb> <target> <scope>` (legacy
exact-yes accepted as equivalent).

Roles: Intake is the only ordinary inbox. Notion Custom Agent alone
writes the Morning Brief. Do not name a bot MAIOS.
